ing them again would double count. Annual page:171 reports finance-lease financing cash outflows of 6 US$m and 5 US$m; simple CFO-minus-capex FCF is before that separately classified principal payment.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 255","text":"The receivables table reports 487 US$m gross drawn and 163 US$m availability in the rounded liquidity table. Annual page:62 instead reports 487.5 US$m drawn and 162.5 US$m available; page:150 reports 487 US$m drawn. These presentations are retained as a precision inconsistency rather than silently unified. Core debt calculations use the debt table's gross amount. Conditional capacity is not added to the chart's undrawn committed revolver measure.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 257","text":"Annual page:153 gives 24,319 US$m of scheduled long-term principal excluding finance leases. This reconciles to the 24,581 US$m long-term gross subtotal less finance leases of 262 US$m. It excludes the short-term receivables facility. Thus the chart is not a complete all-funding maturity profile: the separately disclosed FY2025 receivables refinancing exposure is 487 US$m on the debt-table basis, making FY2025 long-term scheduled principal plus that exposure a calculated 580 US$m, before lease cash payments. Finance lease payment maturities on page:172 include interest and must not be added as principal: 20, 21, 22, 23, 23 and 432 US$m for FY2025, FY2026, FY2027, FY2028, FY2029 and thereafter respectively.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 259","text":"### Financial interpretation and non-debt funding review","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 261","text":"**Leverage.** Gross contractual debt increased by a calculated 5,155 US$m, to 25,068 US$m, while aggregate carrying debt increased by 5,130 US$m, to 24,880 US$m. Gross leverage rose from 6.3256x to 6.5744x on the issuer EBITDA definition. Cash netting reverses the direction, producing 4.9323x versus 5.2227x. The creditor inference is not unqualified deleveraging: the cash-netted result depends on consolidated cash retention and accessibility, while debt principal has increased. Management-adjusted leverage is lower, but its 360 US$m of FY2024 additional exclusions are not validated recurring earnings.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 263","text":"**Coverage and cash-flow quality.** EBITDA / cash interest, net improved to 3.2927x from 2.7138x as EBITDA rose while net cash interest payments were broadly unchanged. Net cash interest excludes the burden offset by interest income and is not interchangeable with either 1,286 US$m of net accrual interest expense or the 1,246 US$m interest adjustment in management's FY2024 CFO bridge. FCF after total capex improved to 1,880 US$m from 1,236 US$m, with FCF / issuer EBITDA of 0.4931 versus 0.3926. This is levered cash generation after cash interest and tax, not an unlevered cash proxy.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 265","text":"The improvement is not wholly an earnings-only signal. Annual page:123 reports receivables cash uses of 84 versus 212 US$m and inventory cash uses of 104 versus 261 US$m. Annual pages 56\u201357 attribute the changes to sequential sales/collections timing and easing supply-chain constraints, respectively. These are issuer explanations, not independently tested working-capital forecasts. Annual page:123 also reports net cash tax of 539 versus 260 US$m. The distinction between timing relief, earnings growth and cash tax matters when extrapolating FCF.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 267","text":"**Capital allocation and liquidity.** FY2024 FCF less acquisition cash spend and cash distributions is a calculated deficit of 2,505 US$m, versus a positive 436 US$m in FY2023. This bridge is before other investing transactions, option proceeds, financing flows and FX, not the reported change in cash. It explains why strong operating cash generation did not prevent debt-funded expansion and distributions. Annual page:151 expressly links the September notes and Tranche L proceeds, together with existing cash, to the special dividend declaration.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 269","text":"Reported cash is 6,261 US$m and revolving availability is 843 US$m at year-end. Annual page:55 separately reports conditional securitization availability of 163 US$m and total cash liquidity of 7,267 US$m. Annual page:56 then discloses a **subsequent October 2024 payment of 4,348 US$m** in special dividends and equivalents and presents pro forma liquidity of 2,919 US$m. Subtracting that payment alone from reported year-end cash gives illustrative cash of 1,913 US$m; this is not actual October cash, because it excludes operating flows, the subsequent receivables draw and other cash movements. Annual page:152 separately discloses the October draw of the remaining 162.5 US$m. Neither event is backdated into the financial or liquidity charts.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 271","text":"**Non-debt funding and cash claims.** All balance-sheet rows at Annual page:120 were reviewed for debt classification versus non-debt funding, together with the accrued-liability detail on page:144, customer contracts on page:142 and leases on pages 171\u2013172. Dividends payable, deferred taxes and non-debt detail are not reclassified as financial debt merely to increase leverage, but they are not dismissed as irrelevant to liquidity.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 273","text":"| Non-debt liability / funding item | 2024 / 2023 US$m | Issuer-specific mechanism and creditor consequence | Evidence / limitation |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 274","text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 275","text":"| Dividends payable | 4,216 / source dash | A declared shareholder cash claim already exists at year-end. It materially qualifies cash netting and the headline liquidity cushion; it is not financial debt in the core ratio. | Annual page:120. Subsequent 4,348 payment includes equivalents and does not equal this balance alone; full payable-to-payment reconciliation Not supplied. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 276","text":"| Dividend equivalent payments, current | 180 / 19 | Additional distribution-related liability inside accrued liabilities; not to be added twice to that total. Together with dividends payable, it reinforces the need to separate cash availability from cash ownership. | Annual page:144; no complete settlement roll-forward established. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 277","text":"| Contract liabilities, current and non-current | 168 and 9 / 79 and 8 | Customer advances provide operating funding but require future performance. Annual page:142 attributes current growth to acquired businesses and advance receipts; do not treat all balance growth as organic cash generation. | Annual page:142; total liabilities 177 / 87, with app