a":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 181","text":"## Next module","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 183","text":"### Selected-consumer readiness","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 185","text":"Each module selected in context is judged once below; unselected modules are not activated by this handoff.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 187","text":"| Selected module | Readiness | What to take and why it matters | Gap and required action |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 188","text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 189","text":"| CP-0 | READY_WITH_LIMITATIONS | Retain its source inventory and accept this bounded historical scope as consistent with its routing; subsequent events and incorporated materials remain separated. | Publication cutoff and preparation certification remain open. Confirm cutoff and obtain preparation receipts; reassess only affected evidence if eligibility changes. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 190","text":"| CP-1 | READY_WITH_LIMITATIONS | Retain canonical figures, cash-flow definitions, debt-table basis and financial perimeter; use the transaction narrative to distinguish acquisition, refinancing and distribution uses. | No retroactive replacement of financials with October cash or unsupported acquired earnings. Obtain settlement roll-forward and target bridge only if additional reconciliation or pro forma work is required. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 191","text":"| CP-1A | READY_WITH_LIMITATIONS | Historical business and transaction context is complete within located evidence: recurring aftermarket demand is weighed against acquisition cash use, shareholder extraction and refinancing dependence. | Proposed deal, ultimate control and legal permissions remain ununderwritten. Obtain deal materials, proxy/control evidence and operative documents before expanding those conclusions. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 193","text":"Return this fact pack to CP-OS with the canonical financial handoff. Committee use is appropriate for a qualified historical credit snapshot, not a fully underwritten proposed transaction or independent covenant opinion. Preserve the high extraction-risk driver, the distinction between completed action and legal capacity, the receivables conflict, and all subsequent-event labels. No peer ranking, instrument recommendation or expected recovery conclusion is made.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null}],"limitation":"Actual analytical handoff; underlying source qualifications and scope remain.","extractor":"literal-markdown-lines","extraction_status":"complete","coverage":[]}],"analytical_qualification":"partial","native_host_qualification":"unrun","responsibilities":{"modules":25,"alternates":16},"rejected_count":0,"run_display":{"as_of":"30 Sep 2024"},"nav":[{"module_id":"CP-0","title":"Source readiness","aliases":["CP-PARSE"],"number":1,"in_pathway":true,"color":"#9AA0B4","glyph":"candidate","word":"Candidate"},{"module_id":"CP-1","title":"Canonical data foundation","aliases":[],"number":2,"in_pathway":true,"color":"#0017E5","glyph":"candidate","word":"Candidate"},{"module_id":"CP-1A","title":"Business transaction fact pack","aliases":["CP-2C"],"number":3,"in_pathway":true,"color":"#2B8FD6","glyph":"candidate","word":"Candidate"}],"report":{"schema_version":"report-view/1","pathway":{"id":"credit_snapshot","title":"TransDigm Group Incorporated \u2014 Credit Snapshot","question":"Should we own this issuer, in which instrument, and why?","requested_modules":["CP-0","CP-1","CP-1A"],"blocks":["company-operating-model","model-chart-strip","financials-credit-metrics","company-profile","transaction-summary"]},"call":[{"kind":"na","label":"Assessment","value_text":"Assessment pending","meter":null,"ref_id":null,"direction":null,"line":false}],"call_withheld":"not_requested","blocks":[{"block_id":"company-operating-model","title":"Company and operating model","owner":"CP-1A","fig_id":null,"tags":[],"state":"populated","kind":"keyvalue","scale":null,"row_header":"Fact area","columns":["Category","Located evidence and measure","Risk mechanic","Credit implication and limitation"],"rows":[{"row_id":"r0","label":"Products, customers and channels","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C302","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual pages 5\u20136: \u201cPower & Control, Airframe and Non-aviation\u201d; product descriptions include actuators, pumps, valves and power systems, latching and locking devices, safety restraints, cockpit systems and testing equipment. Page:6 identifies airlines, maintenance suppliers, OEM/system suppliers and military buying agencies.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C302","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Multiple product families connect original equipment installation to later maintenance and replacement sales; segment economics need not move together.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C302","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Diversification reduces dependence on one component family, not common aviation demand. Segment-level earnings are management-adjusted, not separate GAAP cash flows.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C302","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r1","label":"Installed-base revenue model","cells":[{"text":"Management Language","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C303","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual page:4: \u201cOnce our parts are designed into and sold on a new aircraft, we generate net sales from aftermarket consumption over the life of that aircraft\u201d; management estimates approximately 55% of FY2024 sales from aftermarket and approximately 90% from proprietary products.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C303","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Installed parts create repeat replacement demand; proprietary design and qualification can discourage substitution.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C303","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Supports revenue durability, not a subscription, guaranteed purchase commitment or independently verified competitive position.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C303","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r2","label":"Pricing and gross-margin resilience","cells":[{"text":"Management Language","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C304","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual page:5: \u201cpricing our highly engineered value-added products to fairly reflect the value we provide\u201d; page:12: \u201ccommercial aftermarket net sales have historically produced higher gross profit margins than net sales to commercial OEMs.\u201d Price realization measure: Not disclosed in reviewed evidence.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C304","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Pricing and aftermarket mix may offset cost pressure, but mix shifts can lower gross profit even when unit demand improves.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C304","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Monitor realized price, unit volume and mix separately. No automatic pass-through or quantified pricing power is established.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C304","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r3","label":"Volume drivers and visibility","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C305","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual page:9: commercial aftermarket demand depends on installed OEM base, RPKs, fleet size and age, warranty exposure and airline profitability; defense depends on budgets, campaigns and political pressures. Page:11: \u201cit is difficult to accurately predict the OEM build rates for 2025.\u201d Contracted backlog measure: Not disclosed in reviewed evidence.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C305","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Utilization drives replacement; OEM schedules drive advance component deliveries; government order timing can decouple defense sales from budget headlines.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C305","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Long product lives do not establish near-term revenue certainty. Require channel-based downside monitoring rather than extrapolating one quarter.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C305","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r4","label":"Customer concentration","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C306","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual page:9: \u201cOur top ten customers for fiscal year 2024 accounted for approximately 42% of our net sales\u201d; \u201cNone of our customers individually accounted for greater than 10%\u201d.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C306","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"No single dominant direct customer is disclosed, but collective concentration and shared underlying platforms remain relevant; distributors can obscure ultimate end-customer exposure.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C306","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Direct-customer diversification is not proof of ultimate platform diversification. No look-through customer/platform exposure schedule supplied.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C306","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r5","label":"Manufacturing and cost structure","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C307","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual page:8: \u201cWe maintain approximately 120 manufacturing facilities\u201d; engineering is recorded in cost of sales and selling and administrative expense, and R&D in selling and administrative expense. Page:12 describes supplier delays and increased raw-material and labor costs; page:13 says certification can \u201cprevent efficient replacement of a supplier\u201d. Fixed/variable cost split: Not disclosed.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C307","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Multi-site manufacturing and engineering sustain design positions, but qualified-input shortages can interrupt shipments and absorb cash before customer payment.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C307","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Stress margins and working capital together. No quantified operating-leverage or rapid supplier-substitution assumption is supported.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C307","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r6","label":"Cash conversion and working capital","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C308","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual page:124: \u201cA substantial portion of the Company's revenue is recorded at a point in time basis.\u201d Page:142: contract assets represent performance before billing; contract liabilities are customer payments before performance. Page:141 says payment terms vary and do not contain a significant financing component. Standard customer payment days: Not disclosed.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C308","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Revenue recognition, billing and collection do not coincide for every contract; advances fund operations but entail performance obligations.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C308","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Earnings growth is not automatically cash generation. Track contract assets, collections and acquired balances; do not treat customer advances as free creditor cash.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C308","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r7","label":"Capital spending and operating cash","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C309","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"CP-1 canonical FY2024 figures: CFO USD 2,045 million, capex USD 165 million, FCF after total capex USD 1,880 million; underlying Annual page:123 labels \u201cNet cash provided by operating activities\u201d and \u201cCapital expenditures\u201d. Annual page:56 describes automation and operating-strategy projects. Maintenance/growth split: Not disclosed.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C309","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Cash generated after total capex is available before acquisition and shareholder cash uses; simple FCF does not isolate minimum reinvestment.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C309","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Historical cash generation supports debt service, but does not establish sustainable maintenance-only FCF. No FY2025 capex forecast is adopted.","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C309","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"}],"style":"row"},{"row_id":"r8","label":"Revenue disclosure limits","cells":[{"text":"Documentary Fact","prov":"cited","ref_id":"C310","gap_ref":null,"unit_class":"text","state":"known"},{"text":"Annual pages 141\u2013142 apply the practical expedient not to disclose remaining performance