anually mapped from their directly read source pages; no machine-extraction acceptance or visual inspection is claimed. Reads stopped after the selected annual financial context and relevant notes were obtained."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C270","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 56"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The base is the reported consolidated annual comparison, with gross contractual debt including receivables securitization and finance leases, and the issuer's net-income-based EBITDA as the primary denominator. Cash generation improved, but gross leverage rose and distributions materially constrain the apparent year-end liquidity cushion. Management-adjusted earnings and subsequent dividend-adjusted liquidity are separate supplementary views, not replacements for the reported base."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C271","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 140"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Printed dashes above are source presentation, not missing user inputs and not operands silently filled with zero. On Annual page:123, common-stock repurchases and revolving-credit repayment are also printed as dashes in both selected years. They do not represent an omitted material cash outflow. All newly aggregated values are explicitly calculated below."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C272","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 176"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Annual page:71 states \u201cNeither EBITDA nor EBITDA As Defined is a measurement of financial performance under U.S. GAAP.\u201d The primary EBITDA starts with consolidated net income, not parent-attributable net income, common-stockholder earnings or operating income. Because refinancing and other non-operating results remain in net income, adding total D&A to operating income is a different measure: calculated 3,843 US$m in FY2024 and 3,191 US$m in FY2023, not the issuer's 3,813 US$m and 3,148 US$m. Do not silently interchange these denominators."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C273","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 192"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Annual page:70 explicitly cautions that EBITDA As Defined excludes cash integration costs and neither earnings measure captures interest, tax or asset-replacement cash requirements. Accordingly, adjusted leverage is supplementary. The evidence supports exact bridge arithmetic, not blanket acceptance of the add-backs as one-off or achievable savings. No independent normalized EBITDA, annualized acquired earnings or pro forma covenant EBITDA is asserted."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C274","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 196"},{"name":"Quote","value":"All entries below are reported US$m for the same consolidated annual durations. Annual page:164 provides net sales to external customers and the segment-to-consolidated reconciliation; page:163 states segment performance uses EBITDA As Defined. No segment is excluded or counted twice, and corporate costs are deducted rather than treated as a separate earnings-producing segment."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C275","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 219"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Gross and carrying amounts are distinct. Annual pages 144\u2013145 print short-term securitization separately from the long-term debt subtotal. The primary gross-debt aggregate adds both and includes finance leases and government refundable advances; operating lease liabilities are excluded. That basis is consistent across the two years but need not match agency, covenant or market conventions."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C276","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 253"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Annual page:153 says adjusted Term SOFR on the existing term loans is not subject to a floor. Annual page:55 reports approximately 77% of gross debt fixed rate after the issuer's hedging framework; this is an issuer statement, not a newly reconstructed hedge-adjusted exposure calculation. Operating leases remain operating expenses; finance leases are already in debt, and adding them again would double count. Annual page:171 reports finance-lease financing cash outflows of 6 US$m and 5 US$m; simple CFO-minus-capex FCF is before that separately classified principal payment."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C277","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 255"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The receivables table reports 487 US$m gross drawn and 163 US$m availability in the rounded liquidity table. Annual page:62 instead reports 487.5 US$m drawn and 162.5 US$m available; page:150 reports 487 US$m drawn. These presentations are retained as a precision inconsistency rather than silently unified. Core debt calculations use the debt table's gross amount. Conditional capacity is not added to the chart's undrawn committed revolver measure."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C278","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 257"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Annual page:153 gives 24,319 US$m of scheduled long-term principal excluding finance leases. This reconciles to the 24,581 US$m long-term gross subtotal less finance leases of 262 US$m. It excludes the short-term receivables facility. Thus the chart is not a complete all-funding maturity profile: the separately disclosed FY2025 receivables refinancing exposure is 487 US$m on the debt-table basis, making FY2025 long-term scheduled principal plus that exposure a calculated 580 US$m, before lease cash payments. Finance lease payment maturities on page:172 include interest and must not be added as principal: 20, 21, 22, 23, 23 and 432 US$m for FY2025, FY2026, FY2027, FY2028, FY2029 and thereafter respectively."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C279","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 261"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Leverage.** Gross contractual debt increased by a calculated 5,155 US$m, to 25,068 US$m, while aggregate carrying debt increased by 5,130 US$m, to 24,880 US$m. Gross leverage rose from 6.3256x to 6.5744x on the issuer EBITDA definition. Cash netting reverses the direction, producing 4.9323x versus 5.2227x. The creditor inference is not unqualified deleveraging: the cash-netted result depends on consolidated cash retention and accessibility, while debt principal has increased. Management-adjusted leverage is lower, but its 360 US$m of FY2024 additional exclusions are not validated recurring earnings."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C280","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 263"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Coverage and cash-flow quality.** EBITDA / cash interest, net improved to 3.2927x from 2.7138x as EBITDA rose while net cash interest payments were broadly unchanged. Net cash interest excludes the burden offset by interest income and is not interchangeable with either 1,286 US$m of net accrual interest expense or the 1,246 US$m interest adjustment in management's FY2024 CFO bridge. FCF after total capex improved to 1,880 US$m from 1,236 US$m, with FCF / issuer EBITDA of 0.4931 versus 0.3926. This is levered cash generation after cash interest and tax, not an unlevered cash proxy."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C281","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 265"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The improvement is not wholly an earnings-only signal. Annual page:123 reports receivables cash uses of 84 versus 212 US$m and inventory cash uses of 104 versus 261 US$m. Annual pages 56\u201357 attribute the changes to sequential sales/collections timing and easing supply-chain constraints, respectively. These are issuer explanations, not independently tested working-capital forecasts. Annual page:123 also reports net cash tax of 539 versus 260 US$m. The distinction between timing relief, earnings growth and cash tax matters when extrapolating FCF."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C282","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 267"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Capital allocation and liquidity.** FY2024 FCF less acquisition cash spend and cash distributions is a calculated deficit of 2,505 US$m, versus a positive 436 US$m in FY2023. This bridge is before other investing transactions, option proceeds, financing flows and FX, not the reported change in cash. It explains why strong operating cash generation did not prevent debt-funded expansion and distributions. Annual page:151 expressly links the September notes and Tranche L proceeds, together with existing cash, to the special dividend declaration."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C283","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 269"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Reported cash is 6,261 US$m and revolving availability is 843 US$m at year-end. Annual page:55 separately reports conditional securitization availability of 163 US$m and total cash liquidity of 7,267 US$m. Annual page:56 then discloses a **subsequent October 2024 payment of 4,348 US$m** in special dividends and equivalents and presents pro forma liquidity of 2,919 US$m. Subtracting that payment alone from reported year-end cash gives illustrative cash of 1,913 US$m; this is not actual October cash, because it excludes operating flows, the subsequent receivables draw and other cash movements. Annual page:152 separately discloses the October draw of the remaining 162.5 US$m. Neither event is backdated into the financial or liquidity charts."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C284","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 271"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Non-debt funding and cash claims.** All balance-sheet rows at Annual page:120 were reviewed for debt classification versus non-debt funding, together with the accrued-liability detail on page:144, customer contracts on page:142 and leases on pages 171\u2013172. Dividends payable, deferred taxes and non-debt detail are not reclassified as financial debt merely to increase leverage, but they are not dismissed as irrelevant to liquidity."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"7f0578c02be6bce6849863c7105d17f6d09674ed595b86626286e57d61268e3a"}]},{"ref_id":"C285","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 286"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Covenant interpretation boundary.** Annual page:62 states \u201cWith the exception of the revolving credit facility, the Company has