lue":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 190"},{"name":"Quote","value":"| CP-1 | READY_WITH_LIMITATIONS | Retain canonical figures, cash-flow definitions, debt-table basis and financial perimeter; use the transaction narrative to distinguish acquisition, refinancing and distribution uses. | No retroactive replacement of financials with October cash or unsupported acquired earnings. Obtain settlement roll-forward and target bridge only if additional reconciliation or pro forma work is required. |"},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C360","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 191"},{"name":"Quote","value":"| CP-1A | READY_WITH_LIMITATIONS | Historical business and transaction context is complete within located evidence: recurring aftermarket demand is weighed against acquisition cash use, shareholder extraction and refinancing dependence. | Proposed deal, ultimate control and legal permissions remain ununderwritten. Obtain deal materials, proxy/control evidence and operative documents before expanding those conclusions. |"},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C361","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 3"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Establish the business, ownership, operating-model and historical transaction context for **TransDigm Group Incorporated**, as of **2024-09-30**, for the credit snapshot. The comparison is FY2024 versus FY2023, in USD. This is a creditor-oriented historical fact pack, not a proposed financing recommendation, legal-capacity opinion or recovery assessment."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C362","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 5"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The information-availability cutoff is Not supplied (context, page:1). Consistent with the supplied handoffs, the annual filing is used retrospectively for year-end facts; this is not a claim that its disclosures were publicly available on the as-of date. October cash payments and borrowings are expressly subsequent events. No user-designated proposed transaction is supplied."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C363","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 23"},{"name":"Quote","value":"No external research was used. Management estimates are issuer evidence of management's characterization, not independent market verification. Other supplied renditions and interim reports were not used as additional observations. Referenced proxy materials, exhibits and agreements are not deemed supplied merely because the filing incorporates them. Extracted text supports located quotations, not visual inspection or whole-filing coverage. Reads stopped after the module's business and historical transaction context was established."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C364","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 43"},{"name":"Quote","value":"TransDigm's installed component base supports repeat replacement and maintenance demand, with certification requirements providing a plausible barrier to switching. That is an operating-risk benefit, not proof of contracted backlog or immunity from aircraft utilization, OEM production disruptions, defense ordering or price scrutiny. The company's reported aftermarket economics are management characterizations and remain mix-sensitive."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C365","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 45"},{"name":"Quote","value":"For creditors, capital allocation is the principal counterweight: an established acquisition program and documented distributions mean improved operating cash generation need not become debt reduction. The September debt-funded dividend declaration is direct evidence of shareholder extraction; its October settlement must not be folded into September cash. Refinancing and repricing demonstrate historical market access and extend parts of the debt profile, but do not certify future access, legal headroom or unrestricted availability of consolidated cash. There is no proposed deal to underwrite beyond these historical transactions."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C366","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 75"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Proposed transaction \u2014 Insufficient Information.** Type, parties, sponsor, proceeds, debt raised, terms and liquidity effect: Not supplied in context page:1. There is no designated live mandate and no prospective sources-and-uses or underwriting case. The following are completed historical transactions disclosed by the issuer, not a reconstructed proposed deal. The principal operating issuer is TransDigm Inc.; Annual page:151 expressly identifies it \u201cas issuer\u201d and TransDigm Group and named subsidiaries \u201cas guarantors\u201d. The complete obligor and guarantee perimeter is not verified."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C367","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 77"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Acquisitions \u2014 Documentary Fact; completed.** FPT was acquired on March 1, 2024, for approximately USD 57 million in cash; it supplies specialist fuel tanks and flotation systems and is reported in Airframe (Annual page:137: \u201cThe acquisition was financed through existing cash on hand\u201d). SEI was acquired on May 21, 2024, for approximately USD 171 million in cash, including its working-capital settlement; aerial firefighting and liquid-transportation products were added to Airframe (page:135: \u201cThe acquisition was financed through existing cash on hand\u201d). CPI's Electron Device Business was acquired on June 6, 2024, for approximately USD 1,385 million in cash and added to Power & Control (page:133). Raptor Scientific was acquired on July 31, 2024, for approximately USD 647 million in cash and added to Airframe (page:131: \u201cThe acquisition was financed through existing cash on hand\u201d). The filing describes purchases of all outstanding stock; individual sellers and any target financial sponsors are not established here. No sponsor involvement is inferred."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C368","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 79"},{"name":"Quote","value":"CPI's funding is explicitly differentiated: Annual page:133 says cash included \u201ca portion of the cash proceeds from the new long-term debt issued during the first quarter of fiscal 2024\u201d. Cash funding for the other targets is not automatically relabeled debt funding. Each deal consumes cash and adds integration demands; no realized synergy, target annualized EBITDA or acquisition-driven deleveraging is asserted. Annual pages 131\u2013137 leave measurement periods open and state that acquisition pro forma sales and results are not provided on materiality grounds. These are historical cash purchases with incomplete earnings underwriting, not evidence of failed integration."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C369","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 81"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Acquisition financing \u2014 Documentary Fact; issued and drawn.** On November 28, 2023, the issuer raised USD 1,000 million of Tranche J loans and USD 1,000 million of 7.125% senior secured notes due December 1, 2031. The original Tranche J spread was Term SOFR plus 3.25%, due February 28, 2031 (Annual page:146). Page:147 says proceeds, with cash, were used \u201cprimarily to fund the acquisition of CPI's Electron Device Business\u201d. Issuance provided liquidity ahead of acquisition closing; it also added funded debt before a full year of target earnings. These original loan terms are historical, not the year-end repriced spread."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C370","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 83"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Refinancing and amendment chronology \u2014 Documentary Fact; completed.** On February 27, 2024, the revolver was extended from May 2026 to February 2029, commitment increased from USD 810 million to USD 910 million and margin reduced to Term SOFR plus 2.25% (Annual page:147: \u201cextend the maturity date\u201d). The same date brought USD 2,200 million of 6.375% secured notes due March 1, 2029 and USD 2,200 million of 6.625% secured notes due March 1, 2032. Page:147 says proceeds were used to repurchase the secured notes due 2026; page:149 dates redemption of all USD 4,400 million to March 28, 2024, at par plus accrued interest. This addresses a nearer maturity but is refinancing, not principal deleveraging."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C371","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 85"},{"name":"Quote","value":"On March 22, 2024, Tranche I was repriced to Term SOFR plus 2.75%, and approximately USD 1,708 million of Tranche H due February 2027 was replaced with Tranche K due March 22, 2030 at Term SOFR plus 2.75% (Annual page:148: \u201crepaid in full\u201d and \u201creplaced such loans\u201d). A USD 550 million additional 6.375% secured-note issuance due 2029 funded redemption of USD 550 million of 7.50% subordinated notes due 2027, completed April 22, 2024 (pages 149\u2013150). Extending funding while replacing subordinated with secured borrowing changes the creditor mix; filing summaries do not establish the complete collateral-ranking consequences."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C372","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 87"},{"name":"Quote","value":"On June 4, 2024, Amendment No. 16 repriced USD 997 million of Tranche J to Term SOFR plus 2.50% and converted USD 2,644 million of Tranche I due August 2028 into Tranche J due February 28, 2031 (Annual page:150: \u201camended and extended\u201d). Lower margins and longer maturity improve financing flexibility without reducing principal. No coercive exchange, priming or non-pro-rata treatment is established by these disclosed actions."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C373","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 89"},{"name":"Quote","value":"On July 12, 2024, the receivables facility capacity increased to USD 650 million and maturity extended to July 11, 2025, at Term SOFR plus 1.45% (Annual page:150). Page:151 says it is \u201ccollateralized by substantially all\u201d domestic trade receivables. Its borrowing base depends on receivables, so this is separate short-term collateral-dependent liquidity, not an unconditional extension of the long-term funding runway."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C374","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 91"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Dividend recapitalisation \u2014 Documentary Fact; debt issued and dividend declared before year-end, cash settlement subsequent.** On September 19, 2024, USD 1,500 million of 6.00% secured notes due January 15, 2033 and USD 1,500 million of Tranche L at Term SOFR plus 2.50%, due January 19, 2032, were issued; Tranche L was fully drawn (Annual pages 54 and 151). Page:151 explicitly links both issues and cash on hand to the special dividend declaration. Annual page:54 states that approximately USD 4,348 million of cash payments were funded by USD 3,000 million of new secured debt plus existing cash, and \u201cThese payments were made in October 2024.\u201d The declaration and debt belong to year-end facts; payment does not. New secured claims financed shareholder cash extraction rather than a new operating asset."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C375","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 93"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Earlier distribution \u2014 Documentary Fact; paid during FY2024.** On November 27, 2023, the issuer paid a USD 35.00 per-share special dividend and eligible option equivalents; approximately USD 2,020 million was funded by existing cash (Annual page:54). This is cash extraction but is not separately labeled debt funded. CP-1's FY2024 total distribution cash-flow figure includes other equivalents and is not identical to this event amount."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C376","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 95"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Subsequent events \u2014 Documentary Fact; excluded from year-end balances.** In addition to the October dividend settlement, the remaining USD 162.5 million of receivables availability was drawn in October (Annual page:152: \u201cSubsequent Event\u201d). Annual page:56 presents issuer pro forma liquidity after the dividend, rather than an actual October balance. CP-1's illustrative cash after that payment alone is USD 1,913 million; it excludes other subsequent flows and is not actual post-payment cash. These events qualify, but do not replace, the reported year-end liquidity."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C377","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 99"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Each topic below has no behavior type, funding-source field or legal-capacity-link field: those fields are intentionally not applicable to topic rows. Specific actions are separately recorded in the behavior register. Evidence quality concerns the dated issuer evidence, not certainty that management's statements will prove correct."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C378","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 122"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The governance rubric was applied through the supplied scoring tool to these evidence-based topics and flags. Its qualitative risk-level output is **High**, driven by documented shareholder extraction. No numerical governance score is asserted. This is an issuer-action assessment, not a judgment about individuals, a sponsor identity, or missing information. Support behavior, legal capacity and affiliate leakage remain unassessed rather than adversely inferred; tool scoring does not certify the evidence."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C379","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 147"},{"name":"Quote","value":"One inherited numerical presentation conflict is retained as **logged, not reconciled**. Annual page:62 states: \u201cthe total drawn on the Securitization Facility is $487.5 million, resulting in $162.5 million available to be drawn.\u201d Annual page:150 instead states: \u201cthe total drawn on the Securitization Facility is $487 million.\u201d Annual page:55 prints \u201cAvailability on Securitization Facility 163\u201d in USD millions. These differing precisions are quoted without averaging, choosing a true balance or declaring equivalence. CP-1 preserves its debt-table basis; this module does not create an exact liquidity sum or borrowing-base calculation from these spans. Obtain a dated agent balance and eligibility certificate before precise runway work."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C380","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 149"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Different distribution presentations are not silently reconciled: CP-1 retains the annual cash-flow aggregate separately from the November event amount, year-end payable and October settlement. Those quantities cover different timing and components. Their exact roll-forward remains a gap, not an invented conflict resolution. No other contradiction was established in the bounded read scope; this is not an exhaustive conflict clearance."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfceea5b2"}]},{"ref_id":"C381","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1A"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 153"},{"name":"Quote","value":"No new financial arithmetic was performed. Monetary transaction amounts, dates, coupons and margins above are direct source disclosures. The following are references to accepted CP-1 facts, not recalculations or new covenant measures."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"07ccccb4746145afa4449b1b450050463782c3069199127ef051670bfc